## Payload analysis

| Spec | Value | Source |
|------|-------|--------|
| GVM | 3,500 kg | factory |
| Kerb weight | 2,775 kg | Nick (corrected from web's 2,710) |
| **Factory payload** (GVM − kerb) | **725 kg** | derived |

Payload = everything added on top of the bare vehicle: **accessories + fitout + people + cargo +
towball download**.

### Accessory / fitout weight on the vehicle

| Item | Weight (kg) | Source |
|------|-------------|--------|
| Bull Bar (RAID) inc light bar | 65 | Nick / Ironman-confirmed (63 bar) |
| Canopy (Glass) | 65 | Nick / Ironman-confirmed |
| Drawers | 70 | Nick |
| Roof Racks (RAID) | 25 | Nick |
| Fridge | 30 (empty; +10–15 loaded) | Nick |
| Floor mats / seat covers / tint / dash cam | ~10 | estimate |
| Sport rims (swap for factory 18s) | ~0 net | estimate |
| BYD AC charger (wall-mounted) | 0 | not on vehicle |
| **Total** | **~265 kg** | — |

### Result

```
Factory payload:           725 kg
Less accessories+fitout:  −265 kg
Payload remaining:        ~460 kg
```

**~460 kg remaining** for occupants, remaining gear, and towball download.

| Realistic load | Payload used | Remaining |
|----------------|-------------|-----------|
| Just Nick (~90 kg) | 90 | ~370 kg |
| Nick + 1 + dog (~190 kg) | 190 | ~270 kg |
| Nick + 1, loaded trip (water, recovery, full fridge) | ~300 | ~160 kg |

Tight only at 4 adults or heavy towing. Towing near the 2,500 kg braked limit adds ~250 kg towball
download — that would put the truck near/over GVM with a full cabin.

**GVM upgrade lever:** Ironman 4x4 upgrade lifts GVM to 3,850 kg → factory payload becomes 1,075 kg
→ **~810 kg remaining** after this exact build.

